    "https://employment.potsdam.edu/postings/5509": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "SUNY Potsdam Employment Site | Lecturer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Lecturer Bookmark this Recruitment Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please submit: Cover Letter CV Teaching Philosophy List of 3 references with contact information, including email addresses (other document 1) Posting Details Position Information Posting Number: U - 00658 Position Title: Lecturer Local Title: Lecturer - Teacher Education Job Category Faculty FLSA Classification: Obligation: Calendar Year If College Year, Please fill in period of no obligation: Position Type Temporary Appointment Start date: 09/01/2026 Appointment End date : 08/31/2027 Salary: $70,000 - $72,000 Salary Grade: Full Time or Part Time: Full Time If Part-Time, fill in %: Benefits Summary UUP Fulltime Employee Benefits Summary Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program ( PSLF ) Department Information Department: TEACHER EDUCATION Division Academic Affairs Search Contact Information Search Contact(s): Dr. Laura Brown Chair, Teacher Education Department Search Contact Phone/Extension: Search Contact Email: brownla@potsdam.edu Search Contact Fax: Posting Text Job Summary/Basic Function: The School of Education and Professional Studies at the SUNY College at Potsdam invites applications for a full-time (12-month) non-tenure-track Lecturer position of Elementary Education in the Department of Teacher Education. With a commitment to enhancing diversity and equity for all students, this position focuses on excellence in teaching while providing opportunities to purposely engage with P-12 education partners. The successful candidate will be responsible for supporting curricula and teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses for SUNY Potsdam’s Elementary Education programs during the fall, spring and summer semesters. The successful candidate will also be responsible for supervising teacher candidates in practicum and/or student teaching placements. While a variety of instructional modalities may be required, including online, this is a residential position at the SUNY Potsdam campus. Additional duties of the position will include participation in department and program meetings; participation in faculty governance; contributing to the assessment and accreditation activities of the School and College; and participation in partnership advisory committees. Online, evening, weekend, and/or off-site teaching may be required. Application review will begin immediately. Job Requirements & Essential Functions of the Job: A successful candidate will: Maintain a teaching/supervision load of no more than 15 credit hours per semester (fall and spring) within the candidate’s disciplinary area; Conduct administrative duties and maintain a teaching load during the summer within the candidate’s disciplinary area; Assist with the tracking of teacher candidates’ knowledge, skills, and dispositions; Collaborate with assessment personnel and program/department faculty to assist in collecting assessment data and contributing to program reports related to assessment and accreditation timelines (i.e., Specialty Program Assessment ( SPA ) reports, CAEP , Campus Assessment Cycle); Attend relevant department and program meetings in keeping with roles and responsibilities; Participate in faculty governance; Engage in professional service appropriate to rank; and Actively participate in student retention and recruitment activities. Required Qualifications: A successful candidate will have: 1. Earned a master’s degree in education or a closely related field from an accredited institution; 2. At least 3 years of successful classroom teaching in a P-6 setting; 3. Taught courses at the college level; and 4. Competence in using a variety of educational technologies, including learning management systems (e.g., Brightspace, Teams). We are seeking candidates who possess communication and interpersonal skills to work effectively with a diverse array of students, faculty, and staff. Candidates must also demonstrate a commitment to creating, fostering and sustaining an inclusive environment in and out of the classroom. We are, especially, seeking candidates who have the desire to teach and/or learn to teach a varied and evolving curriculum. Preferred Qualifications: Preference will be given to candidates who have: 1. Experience working with pre-service education students; 2. Supervised classroom field practicum and student teaching experiences; 3. Designed and/or taught classes in an online or hybrid environment; 4. Experience collaborating with various departments or community partners to foster success of underrepresented groups; and 5. Have knowledge of assessment and accreditation processes. Supervisor: Dr. Laura Brown Location: Satterlee Hall, SUNY Potsdam Posting Detail Information Close Date: Open Until Filled Yes EEO Information SUNY Potsdam is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race including traits historically associated with race, color, national origin including ancestry, religion, creed, age, disability, sex, gender identity or expression, actual or perceived sexual orientation, citizenship or immigration status, familial status, marital status, pregnancy, genetic information, predisposing genetic characteristics, military status, domestic violence victim status, criminal conviction, or any other characteristic protected under applicable state or federal law. All qualified applicants with disabilities may be entitled to reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York State Human Rights Law, or other applicable state and federal laws. We will consider requests for reasonable accommodation from qualified applicants with disabilities in completing this application or to otherwise participate in the application process, or, should they be selected to be interviewed, to facilitate their interview. Applicants with disabilities may contact Human Resources to discuss, in confidence, any request for reasonable accommodations. Executive Order 161: Pursuant to Executive Order 161, no State entity, as defined by the Executive Order, is permitted to ask, or mandate, in any form, that an applicant for employment provide his or her current compensation, or any prior compensation history, until such time as the applicant is extended a conditional offer of employment with compensation. If such information has been requested from you before such time, please contact the Governor’s Office of Employee Relations at (518) 474-6988 or via email at info@goer.ny.gov<mailto:info@goer.ny.gov>. All people with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Special Instructions to Applicants: Please submit: Cover Letter CV Teaching Philosophy List of 3 references with contact information, including email addresses (other document 1) Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this opening? Please be specific. (Open Ended Question) * If you heard about this job posting on social media, please indicate what platform: Facebook LinkedIn Instagram Other Not Applicable Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Other Document 1 (Refer to job posting detail information for special instructions.) Optional Documents © 2020 SUNY Potsdam The State University of New York at Potsdam, all rights reserved. 44 Pierrepont Avenue | Potsdam, NY 13676 | 315-267-2000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
