    "https://employment.potsdam.edu/postings/5551": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "SUNY Potsdam Employment Site | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Assistant Professor Bookmark this Recruitment Request Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates should submit: (1) a cover letter describing how their experience and qualifications align with the position requirements; (2) a current curriculum vitae (CV); (3) a written Teaching Philosophy detailing the candidate’s approach to teaching pre-professional performers, conductors, entrepreneurs and music educators, (4) links to at least three representative videos that include both rehearsal and performance footage; and (5) the names and contact information of three professional references. The cover letter and CV should also address the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and interest in a teaching area beyond orchestral conducting. Additional materials may be requested from candidates selected to advance in the search process. For fullest consideration, application materials should be submitted by January 15, 2027. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number: U - 00668 Position Title: Assistant Professor Local Title: Assistant Professor, Director of Orchestras Job Category Faculty FLSA Classification: Exempt Obligation: Academic Year If College Year, Please fill in period of no obligation: Position Type Term Appointment Start date: 09/01/2027 Appointment End date : Salary: $52,838 Salary Grade: Full Time or Part Time: Full Time If Part-Time, fill in %: Benefits Summary Benefits Summary Department Information Department: CRANE SCHOOL OF MUSIC Division Academic Affairs Search Contact Information Search Contact(s): Charles Guy Search Contact Phone/Extension: Search Contact Email: guycv@potsdam.edu Search Contact Fax: Posting Text Job Summary/Basic Function: About Crane Founded in 1886 by Julia Crane, The Crane School of Music has a legacy of excellence in music education and performance. Life at Crane includes an incredible array of more than 300 recitals, lectures and concerts presented by faculty, students and guests each year. The Crane School of Music is SUNY’s only All-Steinway institution and in 2021 was named one of only ten Yamaha Institution of Excellence programs nationally. The Crane School of Music offers rigorous programs with a strong emphasis on performance and practice, in a tightknit atmosphere. The over 400 students benefit from working closely with our distinguished and dedicated full-time faculty of artists, teachers and scholars. About SUNY Potsdam Established in 1816, Potsdam is one of America’s first 50 colleges. With more than 200 years of excellence to draw upon, SUNY Potsdam is dedicated to providing transformational student-centered experiences, in a rigorous and highly personalized educational environment, building on our unique culture of creativity and inclusivity. Students, faculty and alumni alike benefit from the spectacular natural beauty of our surroundings here in the foothills of the Adirondacks. Now in its third century, SUNY Potsdam aspires to be a leader in applied learning, scholarship and service. The Crane School of Music at SUNY Potsdam seeks highly qualified candidates for the position of Assistant Professor, Director of Orchestras. Successful candidates will bring creative and innovative approaches to the study of music, and will demonstrate the capacity to recruit and teach students with diverse interests and backgrounds. Preference will be given to candidates with additional expertise in one or more of the areas listed under Minimum Qualifications. Application Materials Candidates should submit: (1) a cover letter describing how their experience and qualifications align with the position requirements; (2) a current curriculum vitae (CV); (3) a written Teaching Philosophy detailing the candidate’s approach to teaching pre-professional performers, conductors, entrepreneurs and music educators, (4) links to at least three representative videos that include both rehearsal and performance footage; and (5) the names and contact information of three professional references. The cover letter and CV should also address the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and interest in a teaching area beyond orchestral conducting. Additional materials may be requested from candidates selected to advance in the search process. For fullest consideration, application materials should be submitted by January 15, 2027 . Job Requirements & Essential Functions of the Job: Primary responsibility of this position lies in the artistic and pedagogical leadership of the Crane Symphony Orchestra. Teaching in the conducting class sequence is expected. Depending on the candidate’s skills, interests, and background, additional teaching responsibilities as described in the Minimum Qualifications section will be part of the teaching load. The successful candidate will be expected to maintain or develop a regional and national reputation as a conductor, and to participate in service to the university, school, and department. Being part of a collaborative faculty is crucial, as the person in this position will engage with choral, applied, and conducting faculty. Eventual reappointment and tenure processes will encompass teaching, scholarship/creative activity, and service to the university as well as the broader community. This position may require teaching during evening/weekend hours, online, or at off-site SUNY Potsdam locations. Required Qualifications: Graduate degree in conducting or related field at time of appointment. Demonstrated record of success in conducting at the university or professional level. Demonstrated record of success in teaching, including direction of musical ensembles, at the university level. Expertise in and ability to contribute to an additional field of music based on the candidate’s experience and expertise. Demonstrated support of diversity, equity, and inclusion in an educational setting. We are seeking candidates who possess communication and interpersonal skills sufficient to work effectively with an increasingly diverse array of students and colleagues and who have demonstrated a commitment to creating, fostering and sustaining an inclusive environment in and out of the classroom. Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree in conducting or related field at the time of appointment, or equivalent professional experience. Experience in the teaching of conducting at the undergraduate level. Expertise in and ability to contribute to an additional field of music based on the candidate’s experience and expertise. Potential options include, but are not limited to: Applied studio (violin preferred, other instruments considered) Ensemble leadership of other ensembles, such as a chamber/string orchestra, band, or other ensembles. Accompanying Jazz and/or Popular Music Music Business/Arts Administration Musician’s Wellness Other courses as determined by the School of Music, including in SUNY Potsdam’s General Education program. We are, especially, seeking candidates who have worked with, done research with, or taught under-represented groups and have worked collaboratively across various departments in fostering success of underrepresented groups. Supervisor: Dean Andrew Mast Location: Posting Detail Information Close Date: Open Until Filled Yes EEO Information SUNY Potsdam is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race including traits historically associated with race, color, national origin including ancestry, religion, creed, age, disability, sex, gender identity or expression, actual or perceived sexual orientation, citizenship or immigration status, familial status, marital status, pregnancy, genetic information, predisposing genetic characteristics, military status, domestic violence victim status, criminal conviction, or any other characteristic protected under applicable state or federal law. All qualified applicants with disabilities may be entitled to reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York State Human Rights Law, or other applicable state and federal laws. We will consider requests for reasonable accommodation from qualified applicants with disabilities in completing this application or to otherwise participate in the application process, or, should they be selected to be interviewed, to facilitate their interview. Applicants with disabilities may contact Human Resources to discuss, in confidence, any request for reasonable accommodations. Executive Order 161: Pursuant to Executive Order 161, no State entity, as defined by the Executive Order, is permitted to ask, or mandate, in any form, that an applicant for employment provide his or her current compensation, or any prior compensation history, until such time as the applicant is extended a conditional offer of employment with compensation. If such information has been requested from you before such time, please contact the Governor’s Office of Employee Relations at (518) 474-6988 or via email at info@goer.ny.gov<mailto:info@goer.ny.gov>. All people with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Special Instructions to Applicants: Candidates should submit: (1) a cover letter describing how their experience and qualifications align with the position requirements; (2) a current curriculum vitae (CV); (3) a written Teaching Philosophy detailing the candidate’s approach to teaching pre-professional performers, conductors, entrepreneurs and music educators, (4) links to at least three representative videos that include both rehearsal and performance footage; and (5) the names and contact information of three professional references. The cover letter and CV should also address the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and interest in a teaching area beyond orchestral conducting. Additional materials may be requested from candidates selected to advance in the search process. For fullest consideration, application materials should be submitted by January 15, 2027. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this opening? Please be specific. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Other Document 1 (Refer to job posting detail information for special instructions.) Other Document 2 (Refer to job posting detail information for special instructions.) Optional Documents Media Document (Audio or Visual) Link to Web-Based Material (Use for larger files) © 2020 SUNY Potsdam The State University of New York at Potsdam, all rights reserved. 44 Pierrepont Avenue | Potsdam, NY 13676 | 315-267-2000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
